# Kernel configuration of the mainline family (linux-mainline/): only what differs from Kconfig's
# defaults, as savedefconfig writes it. Edit it by hand: savedefconfig of the merged result would
# mix in the SoC and board parts. tools/mainline/kmake.sh merges it with every mainline
# board's SoC part (system/soc/<soc>/kernel.config) and board part (system/board/<board>/
# kernel.config) into one kernel for all of them. This part holds what isn't tied to a chip:
# filesystems, networking, USB gadgets, input, sound and graphics cores, debugging.
# It also enables drivers for hardware a board may lack (USB WiFi and Ethernet adapters, Bluetooth
# dongles).
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
